name: what is running
after: 16-processes
intro: Two questions you will ask on every machine you are ever handed: what is
intro: running, and which of it is yours. ps is where both start.
---
setup: ps prints a header line and then one line per process.
q: count the running processes, excluding the header line
a: ps | tail -n +2 | wc -l
a: ps | grep -v PID | wc -l
a: ps | awk 'NR>1' | wc -l
why: live-hw
ref: ps
hint: drop line 1 before you count what is left
---
setup: ps's own first column is the pid, with no other tool needed to get it.
q: print only the pid column of every process ps lists
a: ps | awk '{print $1}'
a: ps -o pid
out: ^[[:space:]]*[0-9]+[[:space:]]*$
ref: ps
hint: ps -o picks columns by name; pid is one of them
